WEBVTT

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:49.360
- He was a terrible man. - He was kidnapped?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.770
- Yes. - He was kidnapped by a police officer.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.560
How many bullets did you take out of that pistol?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.030
Seven or eight.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.900
- Was it a Colt? - Yes.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.470
The pistol you took out was a Colt small-sized pistol.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.620
It was a result of a shooting exercise.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.560
What did you take out?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.050
I took it out because I had a dream, but I didn't sleep at all.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.200
Did you all take out bullets?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.220
No, I only aimed at the edge of the target.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.520
Hey, hurry up and look.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.640
It's bright red.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.000
I can see everything clearly.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:59.830
The inside of the bus was getting tired. The bus was getting far away.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.890
The baby was crying like she was going to die.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.680
The woman next to her was crying like she was going to die.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.180
I don't think I can do anything about it.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.360
- I... - I don't want you to say that.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.890
We're not a military unit.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.870
What about you? What about me?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.390
What do you mean?

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.350
We can't just stand there until we're finished.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.350
Let's talk to the officer first.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.590
Don't even think about it.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.610
That was a disaster.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:14.170
- And this girl? - Yes, I think so.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.060
- I'm the head of your school. - I'm from Nagashima.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.930
You've got a pretty face, Mr. Hayakura.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:29.410
You look like you're going to bite me, but it's not a big deal.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.000
It's not a big deal.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.540
I'll check it out.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:42.260
I heard you remember Suri's face.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:46.540
Go to the museum, look up the Tenguchi card.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.630
There's a picture of the whole family, and the age.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.000
The Tenguchi is in the box, and the Morimono is in the box.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.930
- What else? - Gender, sex, no hands, no legs.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.560
That's all.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.970
I have a good idea.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.660
Ask the head of your club to call me.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:28.860
I'll do it.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.640
But it's not enough to make the person who did it suffer.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.000
We have to give it to him.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:43.000
Was there anyone else lying in the bus?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.020
There was a strange person next to me.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.310
Which one? That one or that one?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.340
Yes, the one on the right.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.820
He was holding a pistol in his pocket.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.730
That stinks.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.640
There's a guy named Nagata. He's a womanizer.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.520
This one and this one are nostalgic.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:45.220
This Hakoshi died recently.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:53.400
- Today? - Yes, today.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.660
- This one? - Yes, today.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.740
How did he grow up?

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:01.700
That's strange.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.930
Omi is famous for his life.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.690
He's been around for a long time.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.770
That's right.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.570
He worked at a cheap factory.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.920
Omi is a pervert.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.870
Please give me all the information on this woman.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.060
No, no, no.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.260
Omi knows a lot.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:27.390
I don't know what to do with an expert like her.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.190
I don't know what to do.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.000
Where are you going?

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.450
I know, but I'm not going anywhere.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.860
- I'll do something about it. - Something?

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:40.470
- Let me go. - Anyway...

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:10.080
Your father's sleeping in his room.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:16.280
He's 78 years old.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:22.180
- Really? - He's a real man.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.840
He's showing his face.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:29.640
He's a good-for-nothing.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.750
The ogi is a popular dish here.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:40.500
Here.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:10:00.000
What's the news?

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.670
The killer was surprised by the pistol, wasn't he?

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:15.930
No, I thought it was my pistol.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.910
It's been a long time.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:24.000
Ichikawa, I thought you were dead.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.450
Nice to meet you.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:29.250
But it's better than I thought.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.000
What?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:38.860
I heard from my colleague that you were having an affair and I suddenly wanted to see you.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.660
You knew this man, didn't you?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.900
Well, at this age, I'm not interested in young men at all.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:52.050
It's good to run away from the sea because you like the soil.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:55.050
What are you talking about? I don't mind running away.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:59.320
Really? You must have had a lot of sex on the bus.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:04.520
Give me back my pistol. I won't think about anything else.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:08.000
What are you talking about? Don't give me that strange thing.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.760
You can just take it from me.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:13.320
I don't care if you find it or not.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.160
I'll help you.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.820
This man is a newbie.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:22.640
If you commit a crime before you go out, you'll be in trouble.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.480
If you don't know, you'll be in trouble.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.370
I'll sue you for human rights infringement.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.390
You know what's right and what's wrong.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.000
I know what's right and what's wrong.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:32.500
- What did you say? - Bye-bye.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.350
- You won't do anything. - I'll do something.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:45.890
- But you... - No.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.020
I won't give in until you do something.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.300
Thank you very much.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.240
Be careful of the two buildings at the entrance.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.150
*Whistle*

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.190
That's right. I want to go.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:22.630
I won't go until you go.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.090
I'll tell them I'm a human.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.590
I'm free to go wherever you want.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.090
You want to go?

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.310
I'll go.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:13.490
- What time is it now? - It's 11:30.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:19.150
- Is that young man still here? - Yes, he is.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:25.600
He said he'd eat crab here, so he wouldn't mind if there were less shops.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.120
He doesn't drink, so he'll be fine here.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:33.080
It's rare for a young man like you to say that.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:40.530
I don't know why, but why don't you say something?

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.280
I don't care.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.350
Why don't you say something?

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.940
I'm not drinking.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:07.640
Come on, say "I love you" and say "I love you".

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.120
Say "I love you" again.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.500
- The beer is cold. - That's not the point.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:36.880
I know. That's why you're saying you lost.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.340
But I'm not sure who it is. It's just a hint.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.870
- Yeah. - Then look for it.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:50.810
- The pistol? - It's a smuggler, isn't it?

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:54.480
There's a place where the pistols come from.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:59.600
They sell it there, they borrow money, and they talk nonsense.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:11.590
I don't know. I just know that the police are trying to get away with it.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:16.290
I've heard that the police are trying to get away with it.

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:24.970
I see. Please forgive me. Today is a very special day.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:29.480
I've never seen a murderous detective being chased around all day.

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:48.370
I've been thinking about you for 20 years.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:00.870
- Everybody.

00:26:38.860 --> 00:26:42.200
I want you to take care of her.

00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:44.740
Are you sure you want me to do that?

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:46.370
It's a big house, with a lot of people.

00:26:46.370 --> 00:26:47.260
What are you talking about?

00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:53.350
You want to play with me, don't you?

00:26:53.350 --> 00:26:57.400
That's not what I mean!

00:26:57.400 --> 00:27:00.000
Shut up!

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.530
I heard it.

00:27:04.530 --> 00:27:06.600
I'll call the police.

00:28:19.130 --> 00:28:23.680
Hey, don't you have the guts to get angry?

00:28:23.680 --> 00:28:27.040
You're all in good shape.

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:29.600
I'm not telling you to take your clothes off.

00:28:34.730 --> 00:28:37.690
Don't you want to go to the police station?

00:28:37.690 --> 00:28:44.530
I've been told you can't go to the police station.

00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:51.700
I don't want to go to the police station.

00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:54.500
I want to go to the police station.

00:28:54.500 --> 00:28:57.320
You want to go to the police station?

00:28:57.320 --> 00:28:59.800
If you don't want to go to the police station, I won't let you go.

00:29:04.410 --> 00:29:10.980
I'll be back at 9. I'll wait for you to put the white flowers on your head.

00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:32.630
Thank you.

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:05.280
I'm fine. I'd like to look into it, but I'm a bit worried.

00:31:05.810 --> 00:31:07.370
It's very hot in here.

00:31:07.580 --> 00:31:12.320
It's like we're in a tent at night.

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:37.780
Are these the only pistols you're handling?

00:31:37.880 --> 00:31:40.840
Pistols are a business, after all.

00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:43.400
Have you ever handled a Colt?

00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:45.160
What's a Colt?

00:31:45.260 --> 00:31:47.250
It's about this size.

00:32:05.630 --> 00:32:09.530
- Who's this guy? - You know him. He's the one who did it yesterday.

00:32:09.530 --> 00:32:13.090
- When did he do it? Where did he get it? - I don't know.

00:32:13.090 --> 00:32:16.730
He was there. He was supposed to take it in the morning of the deal with you.

00:32:16.730 --> 00:32:18.470
He took it with him.

00:32:18.470 --> 00:32:23.810
When he came out with you, he was surprised.

00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:36.860
I have a message for you.

00:32:38.720 --> 00:32:41.760
You're so mean.

00:32:42.040 --> 00:32:45.530
You'll get a share when you come back.

00:32:46.130 --> 00:32:50.850
You're so mean that you'll get a little more.

00:32:51.070 --> 00:32:53.390
You're so mean that you'll get a little more.

00:32:53.610 --> 00:32:57.010
You're not going anywhere.

00:32:57.210 --> 00:33:00.000
I saw a man reading a newspaper with you.

00:33:00.060 --> 00:33:02.060
I'm sure she'll be there.

00:33:02.060 --> 00:33:03.980
She'll be there for you.

00:33:03.980 --> 00:33:06.220
Don't be in a hurry.

00:33:06.220 --> 00:33:08.300
They're all sleeping.

00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:22.950
What are you talking about?

00:33:22.950 --> 00:33:25.600
Go get them!

00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:28.470
What are you talking about?

00:33:28.470 --> 00:33:30.000
What are you talking about?

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:43.100
It's not a big deal, but it's very interesting.

00:33:45.090 --> 00:33:49.360
But you're so obsessed with your colt.

00:33:49.940 --> 00:33:56.370
I should have sent you more pistols than your colt.

00:33:58.290 --> 00:34:00.000
I shouldn't have sent you so many pistols.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.530
- But... - I know how you feel.

00:34:02.630 --> 00:34:06.450
But you're the one who borrowed that girl's coat.

00:34:06.550 --> 00:34:09.280
There are many other coats besides yours.

00:34:09.380 --> 00:34:14.930
There was a robbery in Yodobashi.

00:34:15.030 --> 00:34:19.560
The girl who was injured came out from the second floor.

00:34:19.660 --> 00:34:22.990
She's also wearing a coat.

00:34:23.090 --> 00:34:27.610
No way. Don't imagine stupid things.

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:30.000
First of all, it's a murder case.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:37.590
You're not so thin. You've lost a lot of weight, haven't you?

00:34:40.340 --> 00:34:45.140
- I'm still young. - It's just an example.

00:34:45.230 --> 00:34:48.810
- Here. - Half a month's allowance.

00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:51.960
How about a day off?

00:35:21.790 --> 00:35:25.920
- Who is the person who investigated the Yotoba incident? - It's me.

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:30.000
The bullet in this vault is the only one left in the records.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.820
The bullet is not useful unless you have a record of it.

00:35:34.820 --> 00:35:37.920
It's the same as the fingerprints.

00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:40.790
It's the gunpowder that was scraped on the surface of the bullet.

00:35:40.790 --> 00:35:53.070
What happened?

00:35:53.070 --> 00:35:56.170
They shot me here.

00:35:56.170 --> 00:35:57.170
And?

00:36:16.730 --> 00:36:19.140
- It's a watch. - Check it out.

00:36:19.590 --> 00:36:21.960
- Where did you get it? - I'll show you.

00:37:14.590 --> 00:37:22.310
It's a new coat. It's a gift. Take a look.

00:37:40.680 --> 00:37:44.240
- Should I take responsibility? - I don't mind.

00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:56.770
I don't care if you beat or crush a person.

00:37:56.770 --> 00:37:59.220
Are you going to be crushed?

00:38:00.600 --> 00:38:02.180
It depends on how you handle this.

00:38:02.180 --> 00:38:05.940
Your luck is your chance.

00:38:05.940 --> 00:38:09.900
Why don't you let me handle this case?

00:38:09.900 --> 00:38:13.720
I'll ask Mr. Abe to be the chief of this case.

00:38:13.720 --> 00:38:16.110
- You know what? - What?

00:38:16.110 --> 00:38:21.480
In Yodobashi, there's a big boss named Naute from the Sato family.

00:38:21.480 --> 00:38:24.800
- Call him so he can be with you. - Yes, sir.

00:38:24.800 --> 00:38:26.780
And before you go,

00:38:26.780 --> 00:38:30.000
you have to take the pistol case you gave me.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.300
If you wash it again, it may become a souvenir.

00:38:33.300 --> 00:38:35.350
Yes, sir.

00:39:00.920 --> 00:39:02.370
- Is No.18 out? - Yes.

00:39:03.080 --> 00:39:06.500
- Do you know where Yodobashi is? - Yodobashi?

00:39:06.620 --> 00:39:09.670
- No.4, Hiraguchi. - Oh, thank you.

00:39:24.170 --> 00:39:29.890
Excuse me. I'm Murakami.

00:39:31.950 --> 00:39:34.050
Who did this to you?

00:39:34.870 --> 00:39:39.030
Sato.

00:39:40.330 --> 00:39:41.810
- Sato? - What's wrong?

00:39:42.010 --> 00:39:44.810
I was asked to take care of the case,

00:39:45.010 --> 00:39:47.210
and Kumiho and I were told to do so.

00:39:47.410 --> 00:39:48.570
I see.

00:39:48.770 --> 00:39:50.250
Please take care of it.

00:39:50.420 --> 00:39:50.840
Thank you.

00:40:03.550 --> 00:40:05.160
It's about the coat that she lent me.

00:40:05.590 --> 00:40:08.000
I heard it from Mr. Gabu.

00:40:08.240 --> 00:40:11.040
It's rare to find a coat with a coat.

00:40:12.750 --> 00:40:16.550
By the way, what happened to the coat you lent me?

00:40:18.090 --> 00:40:20.390
What happened?

00:40:20.610 --> 00:40:22.050
I don't know.

00:40:24.250 --> 00:40:26.860
It was so hot that I wore a winter coat.

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:30.000
- It's black, isn't it? - You know it very well.

00:40:30.640 --> 00:40:32.340
I know you're a left-handed man.

00:40:32.700 --> 00:40:35.220
What? I didn't know that.

00:40:35.880 --> 00:40:38.450
Let's take a break and think about it.

00:41:19.390 --> 00:41:23.300
Yes, he hit me with his left hand.

00:41:23.360 --> 00:41:26.950
I started shaking.

00:41:27.040 --> 00:41:30.000
Did you shoot yourself in the head with that pistol?

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.250
I asked him if he wanted to marry me.

00:41:32.380 --> 00:41:38.730
- What's his name? - I don't know.

00:41:38.850 --> 00:41:43.820
- He must have seen the notice. - Yes, he did.

00:41:43.940 --> 00:41:47.840
But I couldn't read it because it was so difficult.

00:41:49.710 --> 00:41:52.180
I hate college so much.

00:41:52.480 --> 00:41:57.560
- Who has the notice? What's his name? - I don't know.

00:41:57.680 --> 00:41:59.540
- Kimura? - No.

00:42:02.460 --> 00:42:03.850
Then who is it?

00:42:03.850 --> 00:42:07.510
It's your color when you hide it, isn't it?

00:42:07.510 --> 00:42:09.540
- It's not like that! - Listen!

00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:12.050
- Take it back! - It's not like that.

00:42:12.050 --> 00:42:18.120
The one who hides a man's name is a woman of color.

00:42:18.120 --> 00:42:24.900
Come on, let's all go in by the way.

00:42:24.900 --> 00:42:27.590
I'll take another one.

00:42:30.760 --> 00:42:33.270
- What about Honza? - I don't know.

00:42:35.050 --> 00:42:37.650
I really don't know.

00:42:40.020 --> 00:42:43.330
Do you know where he goes?

00:42:44.340 --> 00:42:49.330
- Where does he go? - I don't know.

00:42:51.680 --> 00:42:59.480
I heard he goes to the baseball field often.

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:03.280
- Is it cheap? - Yes.

00:43:04.550 --> 00:43:08.870
It's been two years since I lost my wife.

00:43:09.320 --> 00:43:11.520
- When did you get it? - I don't know.

00:43:13.720 --> 00:43:15.170
All right.

00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:18.310
Wait until I'm done with this cigarette.

00:43:19.710 --> 00:43:22.280
I'll be fine after I get drunk.

00:43:23.490 --> 00:43:27.400
I'm sorry, but could you find a card for Honda?

00:43:27.830 --> 00:43:29.540
Honda might be hard to find.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.490
The material is enough.

00:43:32.490 --> 00:43:35.080
Which one do you want?

00:43:35.080 --> 00:43:38.790
Which one is the coolest?

00:43:38.790 --> 00:43:44.820
Sato-san!

00:43:44.820 --> 00:43:48.270
Thank you. He's called Tachibana.

00:43:48.270 --> 00:43:57.360
He's got a lot of photos.

00:43:57.360 --> 00:43:59.920
And a big one.

00:44:00.280 --> 00:44:05.280
I don't know much about the police or the investigation.

00:44:05.850 --> 00:44:08.450
I'm glad you gave me that woman.

00:44:08.600 --> 00:44:09.920
I want to get rid of her.

00:44:10.210 --> 00:44:13.760
If I catch the woman and stop her, I'll be in trouble.

00:44:14.430 --> 00:44:16.480
I'm sure I'm right.

00:44:20.280 --> 00:44:29.670
I was holding the black fur coat in my left hand.

00:44:31.180 --> 00:44:34.010
His hands must have been shaking.

00:44:36.640 --> 00:44:39.060
He didn't have to do it, but it was all in vain.

00:44:40.090 --> 00:44:43.870
It's a common thing in Oshiro.

00:44:44.330 --> 00:44:47.910
It's a very serious case for the victims.

00:44:49.710 --> 00:44:52.860
What about your daughter?

00:44:55.040 --> 00:44:56.910
She was robbed for 40,000 yen.

00:44:57.180 --> 00:44:59.800
She spent three years to get married.

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:02.600
I'll have to work for another 3 or 4 years.

00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:05.600
My daughter will be gone by then.

00:45:05.600 --> 00:45:08.860
She's been in the war for 10 years.

00:45:08.860 --> 00:45:12.750
She's crying because she wants to get her back.

00:45:12.750 --> 00:45:15.200
She's a wretched girl.

00:45:42.640 --> 00:46:00.000
I'm a murderer. I'm a liar. I shouldn't have done that.

00:46:08.730 --> 00:46:12.070
I feel like something bad is going to happen to me.

00:47:14.430 --> 00:47:16.840
This photo is better than the one he scanned.

00:47:30.220 --> 00:47:32.660
- You're back. - What?

00:47:33.780 --> 00:47:35.940
- You're back again? - Yes.

00:47:36.100 --> 00:47:47.220
- I want to ask you something. - What is it?

00:47:47.940 --> 00:47:50.700
That night, the culprit came to return the coat.

00:47:51.520 --> 00:47:55.640
But the culprit witnessed me giving it to that woman.

00:47:56.230 --> 00:48:00.000
Of course, he thought I gave it to her.

00:48:00.600 --> 00:48:04.820
When the incident happened...

00:48:04.840 --> 00:48:13.570
You were not only the victim, but also the culprit.

00:48:13.670 --> 00:48:17.800
I looked into it, but there was no sign of the gun.

00:48:17.860 --> 00:48:23.270
He was trying to steal the gun from his wife.

00:48:23.710 --> 00:48:26.260
So I came to return it.

00:48:26.360 --> 00:48:30.000
That's boring. You're not good at this kind of thing.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.230
The next thing we need to do is to prevent this.

00:48:32.230 --> 00:48:34.360
The culprit stole 40,000 yen.

00:48:34.360 --> 00:48:37.120
It's not money that can be used for nothing. It'll be gone in no time.

00:48:37.120 --> 00:48:40.210
What do you think will happen when you use up that money?

00:48:40.210 --> 00:48:41.710
I'll tell you again.

00:48:41.710 --> 00:48:45.190
If you say you'll be out for a week, it'll be a different story if you say you'll be out twice.

00:48:45.190 --> 00:48:47.540
You'll be a bodyguard.

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:48.840
Am I wrong?

00:48:48.840 --> 00:48:49.620
No.

00:48:49.620 --> 00:48:52.900
Then you'll do your best to catch Honda first, right?

00:48:52.900 --> 00:48:54.180
I'm sure he'll be here today.

00:48:54.180 --> 00:48:56.690
If you're a baseball fan, you won't miss this game.

00:49:06.840 --> 00:49:08.830
How many do you think you can fit in?

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:12.000
- 50,000? - One out of 50,000.

00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:15.190
Candy or that? Sweet candy or that?

00:49:15.370 --> 00:49:18.240
- That candy? That candy? - Two, please.

00:49:18.370 --> 00:49:20.680
Yes, 20 yen each.

00:49:22.420 --> 00:49:28.200
#2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7, #8.

00:51:34.350 --> 00:51:34.960
You did this.

00:52:00.890 --> 00:52:02.090
The difficult part is yet to come.

00:52:02.090 --> 00:52:02.890
I'm sorry.

00:52:02.890 --> 00:52:04.230
Suddenly I can only see Honda.

00:52:04.230 --> 00:52:07.590
We have to find this Kanshuu in danger.

00:52:07.590 --> 00:52:10.930
Honda has to think that he has a weapon.

00:52:10.930 --> 00:52:14.020
A pistol bullet can't be like a foul ball.

00:52:14.020 --> 00:52:17.540
We have to get rid of this Kanshuu and catch him.

00:52:17.540 --> 00:52:18.670
But wait a minute.

00:52:18.670 --> 00:52:20.400
I'll think about it.

00:52:20.400 --> 00:52:21.990
The game is still five times left.

00:54:22.750 --> 00:54:24.200
We'll call it to Honda.

00:54:38.990 --> 00:54:48.630
- I'm sorry. - I'll call the police.

00:54:49.190 --> 00:54:58.960
- I'll call the police. - I'll call the police.

00:56:42.860 --> 00:56:45.860
But Honda didn't break this.

00:56:46.060 --> 00:56:49.240
What? The one who took the colt didn't give up.

00:56:49.440 --> 00:56:51.440
He should have done something about it.

00:56:51.640 --> 00:56:52.690
You mean Suzume?

00:56:55.030 --> 00:56:58.520
I'm sorry, but please wash this guy.

00:57:00.060 --> 00:57:03.740
We'll have to wait and see how many days it takes.

00:57:03.860 --> 00:57:06.820
I'd like to see the rain, too.

00:57:06.940 --> 00:57:10.100
We'll have to wait and see.

00:57:10.240 --> 00:57:14.210
Mr. Sato and Mr. Murakami will be in charge.

00:57:16.190 --> 00:57:21.570
Is Shinjiro Yu your brother?

00:57:21.710 --> 00:57:27.440
Yes. He hasn't come home in a week.

00:57:27.600 --> 00:57:29.380
That's not a big deal.

00:57:31.120 --> 00:57:34.940
He changed completely after he was sent back to Japan.

00:57:36.030 --> 00:57:37.550
I feel sorry for him.

00:57:37.850 --> 00:57:41.560
When he was sent back, he stole Mr. Tendai's rickshaw.

00:57:42.110 --> 00:57:45.600
- Then he left. - You shouldn't be so conceited.

00:57:45.730 --> 00:57:48.540
He said such harsh things like you.

00:57:48.650 --> 00:57:51.280
He said it was the end of the world, the end of the war.

00:57:51.470 --> 00:57:54.320
He said you were the only one left in Japan.

00:57:54.450 --> 00:57:59.260
- You're the only one left. - No, I have a bad friend.

00:57:59.360 --> 00:58:00.000
A bad friend?

00:58:00.090 --> 00:58:04.930
Well, a Yakuza came to see me once in a while.

00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:08.760
You know, he has this weird style.

00:58:08.860 --> 00:58:11.040
He's got a bad head.

00:58:11.140 --> 00:58:13.350
- He can't go. - What does that mean?

00:58:13.660 --> 00:58:16.710
He said "Sei-san, Sei-san."

00:58:17.010 --> 00:58:19.120
He was with the army.

00:58:19.220 --> 00:58:22.630
- Do you know where he went? - No.

00:58:23.080 --> 00:58:25.670
Can you show me your luggage?

00:58:25.740 --> 00:58:30.000
Luggage? I don't have any.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:32.500
The box is full of junk.

00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:40.070
Excuse me.

00:58:40.070 --> 00:58:45.510
She's a nice girl.

00:58:45.510 --> 00:58:46.960
But she's too weak.

00:58:46.960 --> 00:58:51.640
Play with her.

00:59:01.760 --> 00:59:04.300
Is your father sleeping in this room, too?

00:59:04.420 --> 00:59:08.450
No, in the room behind it.

00:59:08.570 --> 00:59:09.890
There's a room behind it, too?

00:59:10.010 --> 00:59:12.930
No, he built it himself.

00:59:13.050 --> 00:59:14.720
He paid for it.

00:59:14.860 --> 00:59:16.440
Can you show me the room?

00:59:16.560 --> 00:59:20.290
The room is too small.

00:59:34.250 --> 00:59:47.120
Even if I want to do it, I have too many children.

00:59:47.120 --> 00:59:55.190
How is your life at home?

00:59:55.190 --> 00:59:57.940
It's not so bad.

01:00:00.030 --> 01:00:03.150
Yes, I think it was at home.

01:00:03.860 --> 01:00:05.940
He wouldn't come out even if I asked him out for dinner.

01:00:06.480 --> 01:00:10.850
When I looked at him, he was in the dark room...

01:00:11.270 --> 01:00:13.650
with his head held high and crying.

01:00:13.670 --> 01:00:16.230
I was kind of scared.

01:01:02.840 --> 01:01:03.780
I can't sleep today.

01:01:03.780 --> 01:01:09.570
I heard a cat's voice.

01:01:09.570 --> 01:01:12.720
I heard it in the rain.

01:01:12.720 --> 01:01:18.850
It's a bit sad.

01:01:18.850 --> 01:01:20.960
I don't know what to do.

01:01:20.960 --> 01:01:27.680
I still have a lot of work to do.

01:01:30.410 --> 01:01:31.320
I'm Iwamichi.

01:01:31.320 --> 01:01:35.250
I'm Isamu's son.

01:01:35.250 --> 01:01:51.640
- You're his brother? - Yes.

01:01:51.640 --> 01:01:54.900
- What's this Sakura Hotel? - It's a lie.

01:01:54.900 --> 01:01:56.600
That's a yakuza.

01:01:56.600 --> 01:02:00.000
They say he's the owner of the hotel.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.200
I know you're lying. - No, thank you.

01:02:30.350 --> 01:02:39.230
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

01:02:39.230 --> 01:02:43.050
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:02:43.050 --> 01:02:44.820
I'm here to ask you something.

01:02:44.820 --> 01:02:47.480
What is he doing?

01:02:47.480 --> 01:02:49.520
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:02:49.520 --> 01:02:51.470
I'm here to ask you something.

01:02:51.470 --> 01:02:53.470
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:02:53.470 --> 01:02:55.870
I'm here to ask you something.

01:02:55.870 --> 01:02:58.450
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:03:02.080 --> 01:03:04.080
Hey, it's the police.

01:03:11.120 --> 01:03:15.070
The guy in green got caught, didn't he?

01:03:15.070 --> 01:03:17.090
It's not a big deal, but...

01:03:17.090 --> 01:03:18.910
I did it without permission.

01:03:18.910 --> 01:03:20.910
He let me go without permission.

01:03:20.910 --> 01:03:23.930
It's not about Mr. Midori.

01:03:23.930 --> 01:03:25.980
What? Is it about his face?

01:03:25.980 --> 01:03:29.990
Thank you, sir.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:33.040
What do you want to know about Kaoru?

01:03:33.180 --> 01:03:34.850
I want to know about Yusa.

01:03:34.970 --> 01:03:39.010
He's your friend and the brother of the innkeeper.

01:03:39.130 --> 01:03:40.390
Yusa?

01:03:40.510 --> 01:03:42.770
I heard he was beaten quite a bit by the golden army.

01:03:42.890 --> 01:03:45.530
Don't worry, we won't be beaten.

01:03:45.650 --> 01:03:48.110
Why don't we close this place soon?

01:03:50.230 --> 01:03:57.040
By the way, Yusa, when was the last time you saw him?

01:03:57.160 --> 01:03:59.170
Saturday, 11:00 p.m.

01:03:59.290 --> 01:04:00.000
He was drunk.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.020
I'm glad to see you again.

01:04:02.020 --> 01:04:04.070
How was the cake?

01:04:04.070 --> 01:04:06.070
It was new.

01:04:06.070 --> 01:04:08.070
What was it like?

01:04:08.070 --> 01:04:10.110
It was a good morning.

01:04:10.110 --> 01:04:11.930
Good morning.

01:04:11.930 --> 01:04:13.980
Thank you very much.

01:04:13.980 --> 01:04:17.030
It was a good morning.

01:04:17.030 --> 01:04:19.010
There are many men like you here.

01:04:19.010 --> 01:04:21.210
What was it like?

01:04:21.210 --> 01:04:23.960
I don't know.

01:04:23.960 --> 01:04:25.990
Didn't you wonder what happened?

01:04:25.990 --> 01:04:28.910
What did you say?

01:04:28.910 --> 01:04:30.000
I didn't say anything.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:35.250
What did he say to you?

01:04:35.250 --> 01:04:38.230
He said you were the one who made him go away.

01:04:38.230 --> 01:04:41.120
What did he say?

01:04:41.120 --> 01:04:42.170
I just...

01:04:42.170 --> 01:04:44.280
What did I do?

01:04:44.280 --> 01:04:46.330
I just walked with him sometimes.

01:04:46.330 --> 01:04:49.490
What's the point of being friends with someone like that?

01:04:49.490 --> 01:04:50.490
I'm just a friend.

01:04:50.490 --> 01:04:51.490
Shut up.

01:04:51.490 --> 01:04:54.860
You can't be friends with a man like him.

01:04:54.860 --> 01:04:57.800
What's the point of being with him?

01:04:57.800 --> 01:04:59.010
Huh?

01:04:59.010 --> 01:05:00.000
I don't know.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.890
She's just a little bit different from Blue Bird.

01:05:03.890 --> 01:05:05.930
So...

01:05:05.930 --> 01:05:07.350
She's a girl again?

01:05:07.350 --> 01:05:09.090
She is.

01:05:09.090 --> 01:05:17.470
You said you used her to get closer to your debut girl.

01:05:17.470 --> 01:05:19.990
Yes.

01:05:19.990 --> 01:05:21.120
But what does that mean?

01:05:21.120 --> 01:05:24.200
She has a childhood friend.

01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:27.110
Her name is Harumi Namiki, and she's a line dancer.

01:05:33.450 --> 01:05:35.910
I'm not going to be a servant anymore.

01:05:36.910 --> 01:05:41.560
I'm going to be a servant.

01:06:30.800 --> 01:06:32.240
It's the two of them.

01:08:08.180 --> 01:08:14.890
Namiki, why did you take a rest yesterday?

01:08:14.890 --> 01:08:17.290
My body is a little...

01:08:17.290 --> 01:08:18.520
It's because of the heat.

01:08:18.520 --> 01:08:20.930
Everyone has their own problems.

01:08:20.930 --> 01:08:26.720
And the police are here to see you.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:32.310
I don't know what she's doing.

01:09:07.130 --> 01:09:24.100
Namikun. You know him, don't you?

01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:29.700
He's a childhood friend.

01:09:31.180 --> 01:09:32.750
He's my childhood friend.

01:09:32.950 --> 01:09:35.230
We were friends when we were kids.

01:09:36.310 --> 01:09:38.870
Friends?

01:09:39.210 --> 01:09:42.010
We've only been friends for six months.

01:09:42.210 --> 01:09:44.570
You should be honest.

01:09:44.890 --> 01:09:45.880
I'm not lying.

01:10:06.970 --> 01:10:09.500
What kind of relationship did you have recently?

01:10:10.540 --> 01:10:12.000
What kind of relationship?

01:10:12.060 --> 01:10:14.120
For example, were you in love?

01:10:14.560 --> 01:10:17.230
No, not at all.

01:10:17.680 --> 01:10:19.110
Then you were just a fan?

01:10:20.650 --> 01:10:22.380
No, not at all.

01:10:22.530 --> 01:10:23.870
Then what?

01:10:25.240 --> 01:10:27.110
You came here like a stranger.

01:10:27.890 --> 01:10:29.440
I can't just go after you.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.500
- I knew you were. - Don't ask me that.

01:10:36.770 --> 01:10:47.480
- When was the last time? - I don't know.

01:10:48.300 --> 01:10:55.440
You don't know? What's wrong with you?

01:11:33.040 --> 01:11:38.110
I told the mayor.

01:11:38.110 --> 01:11:43.740
You must be tired.

01:11:43.740 --> 01:11:46.050
Then I'll stay here.

01:11:46.050 --> 01:11:51.770
No, I'll have you go out with someone else.

01:11:51.770 --> 01:11:57.250
Why are you crying?

01:11:57.250 --> 01:11:59.160
I'm tired.

01:12:00.160 --> 01:12:05.020
That girl and I have done something bad.

01:12:05.830 --> 01:12:08.550
When you're tired, you can't help it anymore.

01:12:10.440 --> 01:12:14.180
It's hard to keep your head up.

01:12:15.870 --> 01:12:17.600
If you fail, you lose.

01:12:17.660 --> 01:12:18.940
It's the same with sumo.

01:12:19.580 --> 01:12:22.300
I'd like to fight that woman again tomorrow.

01:12:23.140 --> 01:12:29.060
That's fine, but it's hard to get something out of her.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:34.020
There's nothing more stubborn than a girl who's easy to understand.

01:12:34.710 --> 01:12:37.180
If you let your guard down, it's like a stone.

01:12:39.170 --> 01:12:44.190
Where are you going?

01:12:52.970 --> 01:12:56.420
You guys should come to my house.

01:12:56.520 --> 01:12:57.650
What?

01:12:58.690 --> 01:13:00.000
I'm still working.

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:04.260
- Don't be silly. - Welcome back.

01:13:04.270 --> 01:13:07.430
- Are you Omura-san? - Yes, I am.

01:13:07.550 --> 01:13:10.550
I'm sorry it's so cold.

01:13:10.730 --> 01:13:16.720
- Please come in. - Thank you.

01:13:17.260 --> 01:13:23.300
- I remembered the beer. - Here you are.

01:13:23.330 --> 01:13:30.000
- It must have been hard. - No, I just walked around.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:34.200
I got the first ticket for the 13-year anniversary 25 years ago.

01:13:34.200 --> 01:13:37.540
I don't know how long I've been wearing these shoes.

01:13:37.540 --> 01:13:39.540
You must have a lot of memories.

01:13:39.540 --> 01:13:43.640
Yes, I had a lot of things going on.

01:13:43.640 --> 01:13:51.960
Hey.

01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:53.260
Yes?

01:13:53.260 --> 01:13:54.690
There's nothing sudden.

01:13:54.690 --> 01:13:55.690
Can you carry on with the pumpkin?

01:13:55.690 --> 01:13:56.050
Yes.

01:14:12.730 --> 01:14:18.430
I'm a man of my word, but I'm not a good fighter.

01:14:19.630 --> 01:14:26.210
I'm not a good fighter. I'm not good at fighting.

01:14:30.830 --> 01:14:35.480
"There are no bad people in this world. There are only bad circumstances."

01:14:36.290 --> 01:14:41.200
That's what they say, but it's a pity for us to think that way.

01:14:41.820 --> 01:14:47.320
No, no. We don't want to think that way.

01:14:48.150 --> 01:14:51.860
We often get the feeling that we're being chased by criminals.

01:14:52.980 --> 01:14:57.170
But we must not forget the many sheep that were wounded because of the wolf.

01:14:57.550 --> 01:15:00.000
Half of those sheep were killed.

01:15:00.060 --> 01:15:04.020
If you don't have the confidence to protect the happiness of a large number of people,

01:15:04.020 --> 01:15:06.060
you won't be able to save the police at all.

01:15:06.060 --> 01:15:11.760
Leave it to the novelist to find out the truth about the culprit.

01:15:11.760 --> 01:15:14.480
I simply hate them.

01:15:14.480 --> 01:15:16.060
I don't blame the bad guys.

01:15:16.060 --> 01:15:19.970
I still can't think like that.

01:15:19.970 --> 01:15:22.920
While I was in the hospital for a long time,

01:15:22.920 --> 01:15:26.750
I've seen a human being turn into a beast for a very simple reason.

01:15:26.750 --> 01:15:30.000
You and I have been together for a long time.

01:15:30.190 --> 01:15:35.090
Age difference, age difference, and age difference?

01:15:36.560 --> 01:15:38.530
You said something.

01:15:39.440 --> 01:15:41.300
- App... - App...

01:15:41.300 --> 01:15:43.380
- Appregale? - Yes, yes.

01:15:43.380 --> 01:15:45.330
You're from the post-war era.

01:15:45.330 --> 01:15:47.500
Yusa might be the same.

01:15:47.500 --> 01:15:50.090
You understand Yusa's feelings too well.

01:15:50.090 --> 01:15:52.270
Maybe.

01:15:52.270 --> 01:15:55.700
When I was in Fukui, my rucksack was stolen in the train.

01:15:55.700 --> 01:15:57.000
Oh?

01:15:57.000 --> 01:16:00.000
It made me feel so stupid and selfish.

01:16:00.960 --> 01:16:03.890
At that time, Gouto would have done it in peace.

01:16:04.800 --> 01:16:07.200
But I thought this was a dangerous way to go around.

01:16:07.820 --> 01:16:11.400
So I chose the opposite course and did what I'm doing now.

01:16:13.160 --> 01:16:14.600
I see.

01:16:15.720 --> 01:16:18.500
Well, in other words...

01:16:19.530 --> 01:16:21.640
Applegale.

01:16:21.840 --> 01:16:24.290
There are two types of Applegale.

01:16:24.330 --> 01:16:26.050
The one like you and the one like Yusa.

01:16:26.520 --> 01:16:27.860
The one like you is the real thing.

01:16:28.230 --> 01:16:29.530
The one like Yusa...

01:16:30.510 --> 01:16:33.720
I'm going home now.

01:16:33.990 --> 01:16:35.350
I'm getting bored.

01:16:39.840 --> 01:16:44.370
What are you going to do tomorrow?

01:16:44.910 --> 01:16:46.160
Don't be in a hurry.

01:16:46.470 --> 01:16:50.760
But if you spend all that money, you won't be able to get off.

01:16:51.540 --> 01:16:54.480
I'm only going home and half of it is gone.

01:16:54.540 --> 01:16:56.140
It's been a week since you got back from Hong Kong, right?

01:16:56.720 --> 01:16:59.190
It's only 6,000 yen.

01:17:00.380 --> 01:17:02.760
We'll make you live a month.

01:17:14.110 --> 01:17:15.700
Excuse me.

01:17:18.740 --> 01:17:28.740
Tomi, Tomi, welcome home.

01:17:30.800 --> 01:17:42.230
- Let's do it.

01:18:00.090 --> 01:18:01.830
Well, they call us about it.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.580
She's my neighbor, and she's my mother-in-law.

01:19:02.580 --> 01:19:05.670
It's too late, and my wife hasn't come home yet.

01:19:05.670 --> 01:19:09.920
My husband's gone on a business trip, and he'll be back this morning.

01:19:09.920 --> 01:19:15.140
Hmm... I don't know what's going to happen.

01:19:15.140 --> 01:19:19.140
Look, that's the house where the apricots are growing.

01:19:19.140 --> 01:19:22.440
Apricots are bad for your health.

01:19:40.460 --> 01:19:41.910
I don't understand.

01:19:42.010 --> 01:19:46.680
Did you commit suicide?

01:19:46.780 --> 01:19:53.360
I was the only one who didn't want to show my skin.

01:19:54.900 --> 01:19:59.030
I thought it would be painful if I showed my face.

01:20:00.600 --> 01:20:03.300
He's so familiar with me.

01:20:05.070 --> 01:20:09.300
Maybe it's my fault.

01:20:09.400 --> 01:20:11.170
I don't care if it's your fault.

01:20:49.160 --> 01:21:00.000
I was so stupid to make this tomato.

01:21:02.680 --> 01:21:07.490
But my wife is dead.

01:21:32.140 --> 01:21:41.750
I'm sorry.

01:23:02.430 --> 01:23:04.500
Mr. Sato, what about my investigation?

01:23:04.540 --> 01:23:06.570
Your investigation will only cause confusion.

01:23:06.640 --> 01:23:08.100
You can only rely on the truth.

01:23:08.100 --> 01:23:26.980
It's Nakajima.

01:23:37.070 --> 01:23:40.560
- I knew it. - It's a Yusa's bullet.

01:24:01.470 --> 01:24:05.920
It's not the time to think about it.

01:24:06.160 --> 01:24:09.260
As long as we don't catch Misa, we won't solve the problem.

01:24:09.430 --> 01:24:11.430
We still have five shots left on Misa's pistol.

01:24:21.720 --> 01:24:23.360
Did you get any information? Where are you going?

01:24:23.460 --> 01:24:25.700
I'm going back to my house and I'm going to sleep.

01:24:25.800 --> 01:24:27.360
That's not fair, Mr. Sato.

01:24:27.460 --> 01:24:30.000
If you go back to your house, you won't be able to sleep with us.

01:24:30.060 --> 01:24:32.220
Let me go. It's too hot in here.

01:24:32.360 --> 01:24:34.400
- What about the stars? - They're going to get dark.

01:24:34.520 --> 01:24:36.280
Hurry up!

01:24:38.620 --> 01:24:42.870
- You're really angry, aren't you? - Who are you talking about?

01:24:43.310 --> 01:24:46.440
- Who? - I'm talking about Yudachi.

01:24:46.740 --> 01:24:50.100
No way.

01:24:51.010 --> 01:24:53.680
He's just a nervous cop.

01:24:54.190 --> 01:24:56.150
I'm not nervous at all, Mr. Sato.

01:24:56.570 --> 01:24:59.410
If you say that, you're already nervous.

01:25:07.360 --> 01:25:09.830
I think this is the point of the fight.

01:25:10.420 --> 01:25:11.810
He killed someone.

01:25:11.810 --> 01:25:14.760
The person who killed someone is a swordsman.

01:25:14.790 --> 01:25:18.310
Do you know how a swordsman moves?

01:25:18.610 --> 01:25:20.610
He has a sword in his hands.

01:25:21.240 --> 01:25:23.490
You're so bad at it.

01:25:24.170 --> 01:25:26.760
But the swordsman has a straight path.

01:25:27.530 --> 01:25:30.000
You can only see a straight path.

01:25:30.640 --> 01:25:34.390
He's in love with you. He can only see you.

01:25:35.090 --> 01:25:37.650
He'll come to see you.

01:26:20.540 --> 01:26:23.780
I'm a manager, so I'm in charge of the literature department.

01:26:35.660 --> 01:26:37.310
I want to see Namiki.

01:26:37.310 --> 01:26:42.440
Harubo's off today.

01:26:42.440 --> 01:26:47.450
She's a troubled child.

01:26:47.450 --> 01:26:50.840
She'll be off soon if I tell her.

01:26:50.840 --> 01:26:57.650
She's quiet, but she's a stubborn child.

01:27:04.120 --> 01:27:06.700
Besides, he's sick right now.

01:27:06.700 --> 01:27:09.280
What's wrong with him?

01:27:09.280 --> 01:27:13.560
Well, it's like that every month.

01:27:13.560 --> 01:27:17.960
He always makes me work during that time.

01:27:17.960 --> 01:27:24.950
Do you know who he is?

01:27:24.950 --> 01:27:29.960
Yes, I think it's Koenji.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:34.900
I should have been able to do it.

01:28:07.550 --> 01:28:18.790
Thank you.

01:28:43.150 --> 01:28:44.080
Take care of yourself.

01:29:17.440 --> 01:29:18.620
Don't worry.

01:29:31.310 --> 01:29:36.000
Looks like someone is coming.

01:29:36.000 --> 01:29:43.140
I'd like to ask you something.

01:29:43.140 --> 01:29:46.550
I don't know anything about Yusa.

01:29:46.550 --> 01:29:48.870
The police are very strict.

01:29:48.870 --> 01:29:52.570
Don't say that.

01:29:52.570 --> 01:29:54.210
Don't tell your mother.

01:29:54.210 --> 01:29:58.050
We have the right to say what we want to say.

01:29:58.050 --> 01:30:00.000
The suspect committed a robbery.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:07.200
Does he have the right to do so?

01:30:07.320 --> 01:30:08.920
I don't know what I don't know.

01:30:09.040 --> 01:30:13.410
You're lying. He's still here.

01:30:13.530 --> 01:30:16.000
Yusa brought this match.

01:30:16.120 --> 01:30:19.300
That's right.

01:30:19.420 --> 01:30:23.740
He said he didn't want it.

01:30:23.860 --> 01:30:26.300
Do you know where Yusa is?

01:30:26.420 --> 01:30:30.000
I told you. Harumi.

01:30:30.960 --> 01:30:33.950
I don't know if you really don't know.

01:30:33.950 --> 01:30:38.830
If you really don't know, I won't forgive you if you lie.

01:30:38.830 --> 01:30:44.910
Harumi, Harumi, Harumi, why are you silent?

01:30:44.910 --> 01:30:49.360
Tell me, tell me, Harumi.

01:31:06.880 --> 01:31:10.440
I don't have the time for that.

01:31:11.670 --> 01:31:14.790
I'm going to the hotel.

01:31:14.810 --> 01:31:17.610
- What about me? - You stay in that room.

01:31:18.230 --> 01:31:21.260
He's a great detective about his daughter.

01:31:21.380 --> 01:31:25.440
I'll call him.

01:31:25.720 --> 01:31:28.390
- Do you have a gun? - Yes, I do.

01:31:28.520 --> 01:31:29.800
Put it away.

01:31:30.220 --> 01:31:39.000
Kesa has gone home.

01:31:39.240 --> 01:31:41.080
He'll be back tonight.

01:31:42.740 --> 01:31:58.900
Don't say that.

01:32:00.090 --> 01:32:06.560
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have pampered you when you didn't have your father.

01:32:06.560 --> 01:32:10.930
I don't care. I want my mother to be a fool no matter how much I want her to be a fool.

01:32:10.930 --> 01:32:26.470
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have pampered you when you didn't have your father.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.060
He's a 27 or 28-year-old man dressed like that.

01:32:34.160 --> 01:32:44.700
I see.

01:32:44.800 --> 01:32:55.230
He doesn't want to be praised, so I'll put him on.

01:32:55.330 --> 01:32:58.480
I see. This is it.

01:33:02.780 --> 01:33:05.920
Oh, it's her.

01:33:07.040 --> 01:33:12.100
She was staying for the night, but she never got drunk.

01:33:12.910 --> 01:33:14.920
She didn't bring her partner.

01:33:15.040 --> 01:33:17.510
She was a very popular woman.

01:33:18.260 --> 01:33:24.130
It was the night before yesterday, but she suddenly stopped and called a car.

01:33:24.270 --> 01:33:25.670
Do you know where the car is?

01:33:25.940 --> 01:33:27.910
It's a taxi by the train.

01:33:28.540 --> 01:33:29.960
I see.

01:33:30.890 --> 01:33:33.760
- He was a driver. - Thank you.

01:33:34.520 --> 01:33:37.200
- Who is he? - A police officer.

01:34:00.000 --> 01:34:02.170
Do you want to make us suffer?

01:34:02.930 --> 01:34:04.090
You're the one who's suffering.

01:34:04.210 --> 01:34:07.670
No, I'm not.

01:34:07.790 --> 01:34:10.290
I don't know what Yu-san did,

01:34:10.450 --> 01:34:14.360
but he didn't do anything wrong to me.

01:34:15.290 --> 01:34:20.940
Sometimes he came to my room and looked at me with sad eyes.

01:34:21.310 --> 01:34:25.450
I can't let him catch me with my own hands.

01:34:25.670 --> 01:34:28.090
So you know Yu-san's whereabouts, but you can't tell me?

01:34:30.250 --> 01:34:35.140
Maybe. I know you're going to catch me.

01:34:35.690 --> 01:34:37.350
But I don't want you to catch me.

01:35:02.810 --> 01:35:04.640
Give it back to me!

01:35:08.290 --> 01:35:09.600
Damn it!

01:35:09.960 --> 01:35:13.860
I thought it was better to cut it short.

01:35:13.960 --> 01:35:15.200
Where did you take her?

01:35:15.650 --> 01:35:18.280
I'm waiting for her at Koumetsu.

01:35:18.280 --> 01:35:19.360
Excuse me.

01:35:41.800 --> 01:35:43.300
I didn't know he was so...

01:35:51.270 --> 01:35:56.920
He gave me this when we were walking.

01:35:58.380 --> 01:35:59.730
I saw it in the window.

01:36:05.180 --> 01:36:12.720
He said he wanted to wear such a beautiful dress.

01:36:12.720 --> 01:36:18.760
At that time, he was looking at me with sadness.

01:36:18.760 --> 01:36:22.530
About a week later, he brought this to the dressing room.

01:36:22.530 --> 01:36:25.120
Rumi, really.

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:37.030
I did something bad to you, but if I had the courage, I would have stolen it myself.

01:36:37.030 --> 01:36:39.930
It's not right to show this to the police.

01:36:39.930 --> 01:36:45.040
To buy something like this, we have to do something worse than stealing.

01:36:45.040 --> 01:36:57.790
Harumi!

01:36:57.790 --> 01:36:59.060
Everyone has a bad feeling about this.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:02.110
The world is full of people who steal.

01:37:02.110 --> 01:37:09.150
You said that, didn't you?

01:37:09.150 --> 01:37:11.110
But you're not the only one who steals.

01:37:11.110 --> 01:37:21.360
I was also stolen.

01:37:21.360 --> 01:37:23.140
I'm innocent.

01:37:23.140 --> 01:37:24.800
The world is evil.

01:37:24.800 --> 01:37:26.010
But...

01:37:26.010 --> 01:37:28.010
I'm the one who does bad things for the world!

01:37:28.010 --> 01:37:29.010
You're the one who's bad!

01:37:29.010 --> 01:37:30.000
You're the one who's bad!

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:31.920
I'm wearing an ugly kimono for something delicious.

01:37:31.920 --> 01:37:34.370
I'll win if I do something bad.

01:37:34.370 --> 01:37:35.320
Is that what you really think?

01:37:35.320 --> 01:37:38.590
Then I'm not going to work.

01:37:38.590 --> 01:37:41.370
I can wear this dress.

01:37:41.370 --> 01:37:44.530
Come on, wear it.

01:37:44.530 --> 01:37:52.440
It's hot, but it's hard, isn't it?

01:37:52.440 --> 01:37:53.400
What do you think?

01:37:53.400 --> 01:37:57.240
Here you go.

01:38:02.270 --> 01:38:06.440
- That's alcohol. - I thought I'd pay for it.

01:38:06.500 --> 01:38:12.290
What happened to the man?

01:38:12.410 --> 01:38:17.350
He came home late. He went home early in the morning.

01:38:17.440 --> 01:38:19.780
And then...

01:38:19.920 --> 01:38:22.530
- What about the other man? - Well...

01:38:22.670 --> 01:38:26.050
He took her to the street.

01:38:26.200 --> 01:38:29.890
- What street? - Kintaro, Wakeshita-matsu.

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:31.520
That's right.

01:38:31.620 --> 01:38:33.700
But it was out of tune when I played it.

01:38:33.800 --> 01:38:35.730
Oh, she's a good singer.

01:38:35.830 --> 01:38:37.550
I'll ask her where she's going.

01:38:37.650 --> 01:38:39.810
She's having a performance today.

01:38:39.910 --> 01:38:41.860
- Where? - Musashiya.

01:38:42.370 --> 01:38:47.390
- Where? - It's fun.

01:38:49.410 --> 01:38:51.630
It's fun.

01:38:51.880 --> 01:38:58.320
It's like a dream.

01:39:52.360 --> 01:39:53.810
It's a gold-threaded one.

01:39:53.970 --> 01:39:56.410
Oh, it'll look good on you.

01:39:56.530 --> 01:39:57.420
Yes.

01:39:59.410 --> 01:40:00.000
Let's go.

01:40:00.160 --> 01:40:05.400
I don't want to talk. I want to ask about the guest who stayed the night before last.

01:40:05.400 --> 01:40:08.340
- The night before last? - Yes.

01:40:08.340 --> 01:40:12.260
- Oh, I don't like that kind of guest. - Why not?

01:40:12.260 --> 01:40:16.600
Because he's strange.

01:40:16.600 --> 01:40:19.680
- What's wrong with him? - Yes.

01:40:19.680 --> 01:40:23.880
- I sent him to the train station. - Oh, you know him well.

01:40:23.880 --> 01:40:26.890
- Where did he go? - Where did he go?

01:40:26.890 --> 01:40:30.000
- Didn't you ask him? - No, I didn't.

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:33.180
- Where? - The hotel in Kanda.

01:40:33.280 --> 01:40:35.470
I won't let you go.

01:40:35.570 --> 01:40:45.610
You're so stupid.

01:40:45.710 --> 01:40:49.230
I'll let you go right away.

01:40:49.330 --> 01:40:54.270
Don't say that.

01:40:54.370 --> 01:40:58.930
This is an experiment.

01:41:04.890 --> 01:41:09.990
The pistol Yusa was holding was stolen by my father.

01:41:10.990 --> 01:41:19.400
That's why two people were shot with my pistol.

01:41:20.180 --> 01:41:23.550
And one of them was killed.

01:41:25.380 --> 01:41:27.880
Tonight, we're going to make a big scene.

01:41:28.100 --> 01:41:29.350
Something bad is going to happen.

01:41:46.480 --> 01:41:52.650
It's the police. Haruo Namiki is staying here, right?

01:41:52.750 --> 01:41:54.730
- Yes. - Room 6.

01:41:54.770 --> 01:41:55.510
2nd floor.

01:42:00.350 --> 01:42:03.340
- What about the phone? - It's over here.

01:42:03.430 --> 01:42:22.720
Don't tell them the police is here.

01:42:22.820 --> 01:42:30.000
- This is the only exit. - There's another one in the back.

01:42:30.030 --> 01:42:31.720
- Good morning. - Where's the key?

01:42:31.990 --> 01:42:33.940
- I'll close it today. - Go ahead.

01:42:34.050 --> 01:42:47.630
- It's late. - I'm not in the mood.

01:42:48.330 --> 01:42:50.870
Damn it. I don't have money. I have to go to the police.

01:43:07.040 --> 01:43:10.950
He's a police man, isn't he?

01:43:12.390 --> 01:43:15.110
If he doesn't go to jail, he won't be able to go to prison.

01:44:08.640 --> 01:44:21.220
No. It's Harumi's room.

01:44:23.020 --> 01:44:24.840
Mr. Harumi?

01:44:33.290 --> 01:44:36.490
Wait, it's Murakami, not your husband.

01:44:36.490 --> 01:44:42.300
Mr. Akano, good-bye.

01:44:42.300 --> 01:45:00.000
- If it's about Risa... - Hey, that man...

01:45:00.220 --> 01:45:03.080
If it was him, what would he have done?

01:45:03.080 --> 01:45:04.800
Hello?

01:46:18.910 --> 01:46:23.910
Hello, this is Harumi speaking.

01:46:23.910 --> 01:46:26.190
Sato-san?

01:46:26.190 --> 01:46:29.640
Hello, this is Murakami-kun.

01:47:29.500 --> 01:47:30.000
Give it away.

01:47:58.120 --> 01:47:58.800
How many grams?

01:48:00.320 --> 01:48:06.660
I don't know.

01:48:53.870 --> 01:48:54.480
Let me go!

01:49:04.440 --> 01:49:08.520
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

01:50:44.810 --> 01:50:47.720
Yusaka, I'll be waiting for you at Ohara Station at 6:00.

01:50:47.720 --> 01:50:49.300
I'll call you later.

01:50:49.300 --> 01:50:55.410
Your wife is still here.

01:52:09.500 --> 01:52:10.400
28 years old.

01:52:10.400 --> 01:52:13.000
Shoihasa no Sebiro.

01:52:13.000 --> 01:52:15.680
28 years old.

01:52:30.190 --> 01:52:31.910
He might have changed his clothes.

01:52:31.910 --> 01:52:34.920
Then, a 28-year-old man...

01:52:34.920 --> 01:52:41.060
A 28-year-old man...

01:52:41.060 --> 01:52:44.080
A 28-year-old man...

01:52:44.080 --> 01:52:47.870
A 28-year-old man...

01:52:47.870 --> 01:52:58.320
He jumped out of the car.

01:53:01.470 --> 01:53:07.300
Shoes full of blood.

01:59:32.430 --> 01:59:43.830
*crying*

02:00:09.120 --> 02:00:13.240
Takajima-san told me you got the award.

02:00:13.340 --> 02:00:15.520
No, it's all thanks to Sato-san.

02:00:15.620 --> 02:00:20.610
No, I don't think so.

02:00:22.420 --> 02:00:26.150
But it started with my loss.

02:00:26.260 --> 02:00:28.550
I don't think it's over yet.

02:00:30.120 --> 02:00:34.780
But you know, thanks to you and Colt,

02:00:35.420 --> 02:00:37.480
I was able to get a few pistols from Honda.

02:00:39.690 --> 02:00:48.300
But somehow, I feel bad about the man who killed him.

02:00:49.850 --> 02:00:53.960
The first criminal I caught, I can't forget him.

02:00:55.410 --> 02:00:59.120
But you know, compared to what you're thinking,

02:01:00.090 --> 02:01:02.760
There are a lot of people like that.

02:01:03.180 --> 02:01:07.450
As long as you catch them, you won't have to worry about them anymore.

02:01:10.520 --> 02:01:13.720
What was the name of the girl?

02:01:13.980 --> 02:01:15.300
Harumi Namiki?

02:01:15.370 --> 02:01:16.710
Yes.

02:01:18.330 --> 02:01:23.490
I don't know anyone like her.

02:01:26.450 --> 02:01:27.680
Look outside.

02:01:38.160 --> 02:01:40.470
All sorts of things will happen under that roof.

02:01:42.160 --> 02:01:45.660
And a few people, all of them good-for-nothing,

02:01:46.370 --> 02:01:48.600
will become the conscience of people like Yusa.

02:01:52.940 --> 02:01:56.370
Don't forget that.

02:01:57.580 --> 02:02:00.000
No, if you get better,

02:02:00.000 --> 02:02:11.910
I'll forget about it.
